 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "How did a little dog named Pickles save the World Cup?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.544
  },
  {
   "text": "He's on a walk in London when he drags his owner to a hedge and won't stop sniffing.",
   "s": 2.844,
   "e": 6.663
  },
  {
   "text": "Under the bush sits a lump of old newspaper, tied with string.",
   "s": 6.863,
   "e": 9.642
  },
  {
   "text": "His owner rips it open, and gold flashes inside.",
   "s": 9.842,
   "e": 12.279
  },
  {
   "text": "It's the World Cup trophy, stolen from a London show one week before!",
   "s": 12.479,
   "e": 15.924
  },
  {
   "text": "England hosts the tournament in four months, and without a trophy, there's nothing to win.",
   "s": 16.124,
   "e": 20.314
  },
  {
   "text": "So the owner rushes it to the police, proud as can be.",
   "s": 20.514,
   "e": 23.045
  },
  {
   "text": "But the detectives don't cheer. They question him for hours.",
   "s": 23.245,
   "e": 25.937
  },
  {
   "text": "Because who finds the World Cup on a dog walk?",
   "s": 26.137,
   "e": 28.05
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it gets weirder. Pickles becomes the most famous dog in Britain.",
   "s": 28.35,
   "e": 31.611
  },
  {
   "text": "He gets a medal, a movie role, and a year of free dog food.",
   "s": 31.811,
   "e": 34.771
  },
  {
   "text": "In July, England wins the World Cup.",
   "s": 35.171,
   "e": 36.991
  },
  {
   "text": "And at the victory party, one special guest gets to lick the plates. Pickles.",
   "s": 37.191,
   "e": 41.057
  },
  {
   "text": "The players won the cup. But guess who found it first?",
   "s": 41.257,
   "e": 43.627
  }
 ],
